Yeah, the english sounds tautolgical to me.  But that's not necessarily a
bad thing.  Sometimes we use tautologies to pull the familiarity away from a
word that has come to almost be a name.  "people are people", "haters gonna
hate".  "lo pendo cu pendo" sounds to me like "friends are friends" which
seems like the intent is to remind us that {lo pendo} is not {la pendo} ;)

